# Kyverno CEL mutating path at 16 policies, each writing its own annotation.
#
# Scope is deliberately the CEL arm plus baseline, not all five engines. The
# distinct variant exists only for kyverno-cel, so a five-arm run would compare
# one arm doing 16 distinct mutations against four arms doing 16 identical ones.
# For an A/B of two Kyverno builds that does not matter, and this is the shape
# that A/B should use.
#
# Against cel-mutate-n16 (the selectors variant), the difference is that there
# every copy re-adds the same annotation and the object never grows, while here
# copy 003 writes policy-bench-mutate-003 and a matched Pod ends up carrying 16
# new annotations. Object conversion cost tracks JSON nodes, so this is the shape
# where per-policy object handling is actually loaded.
ENGINES=${ENGINES:-"baseline kyverno-cel"}
POLICY_COUNT=${POLICY_COUNT:-16}
POLICY_MODE=${POLICY_MODE:-mutate}
KYVERNO_CEL_VARIANT=${KYVERNO_CEL_VARIANT:-distinct}
PAYLOAD_PROFILE=${PAYLOAD_PROFILE:-minimal}
TARGET_RPS=${TARGET_RPS:-200}
TRIALS=${TRIALS:-3}
PROFILE=${PROFILE:-scaling}
